2026-10-30T08:33:58.6628238Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6713782Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6721948Z [0m
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6722674Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6723120Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6723312Z 
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6723589Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6724071Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6724346Z 
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6724590Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6724952Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6725116Z 
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6725590Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6726149Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6726595Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6726829Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6726929Z 
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6727086Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6727238Z 
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6727391Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6727607Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6727685Z 
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6727756Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6727846Z 
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6728070Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6728587Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6739291Z 
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6739740Z I will:
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6739879Z 
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6740109Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6740525Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6741309Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6741548Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6741711Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6741896Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6742178Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6742388Z    /root
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6750421Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6750909Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6760482Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6760911Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6761342Z 
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6763406Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6763763Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6779702Z 
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6780179Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6788815Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-30T08:33:58.6789335Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
